<section class="shell">
  <h1>Commenting and privacy</h1>
  <p>The Engineering Journal and case studies welcome questions, relevant experience and thoughtful disagreement.
    Keep comments on topic and avoid posting passwords, API keys, private customer details or other confidential information.</p>
  <h2>Your comments and account</h2>
  <p>Comments and your chosen display name are public. When commenting is enabled, you can use a guest name or one of
    the sign-in options shown in the form, such as Google, GitHub or email.
    Signing in uses the provider you choose; this website does not receive your Google or GitHub password.
    Email addresses used for sign-in are not displayed in the discussion. Essential cookies keep you signed in.</p>
  <p>This website's commenting service runs on AWS using Remark42. It stores comments, account identifiers and profile images,
    and uses technical information such as IP addresses for abuse prevention. Reply email subscriptions are disabled.</p>
  <h2>Spam moderation</h2>
  <p>This website uses OpenAI to help identify spam. Comment text, the article title and relevant parent-comment text may be sent
    for review. Those review requests do not include your sign-in email address or recorded IP address.
    Anything you write in the comment itself can be included, so keep private information out of your posts.</p>
  <p>Clear spam may be removed automatically. Uncertain cases remain visible for the maintainer to review.
    Criticism and relevant technical discussion are welcome. Automated review can make mistakes;
    contact <a href="mailto:benny@bennybottema.com">Benny Bottema</a> if a comment needs attention.</p>
  <p>Private recovery copies of removed comments and daily backups have a 30-day expiration policy. OpenAI API data is not used
    for model training by default; its separate abuse-monitoring retention rules may still apply.
    See <a href="https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/your-data">OpenAI's API data controls</a>.</p>
  <h2>Changes and removal requests</h2>
  <p>Remark42 allows a short editing window after posting. For later corrections, account questions or removal requests,
    contact the maintainer using the address above.</p>
</section>
